{"after":1,"q":"Warm-up 1. What is the m.sg. active participle of <em>ʿ-b-d</em>?","opts":[["<em>ʿābed</em>","Right: the <em>CāCeC</em> pattern."],["<em>ʿbad</em>","That is the Perfect “he made.”"],["<em>ʿābdīn</em>","That is plural."],["<em>ʿābdā</em>","That is feminine."]]},
{"after":1,"q":"Warm-up 2. How would you say “We are going” (<em>ʾ-z-l</em> + <em>-ḥnan</em>)?","opts":[["<em>ʾāzlīn-ḥnan</em>","Right."],["<em>ʾāzel-nā</em>","That is “I am going.”"],["<em>ʾāzlīn</em>","Without the enclitic it means “they are going.”"],["<em>ʾezaln</em>","That is a Perfect form, “we went.”"]]},
{"after":1,"q":"Warm-up 3. Translate: <em>Šāmʿīn-tūn meltā d-Alāhā.</em>","opts":[["You all are hearing the word of God.","Right."],["We are hearing the word of God.","<em>-tūn</em> is 2 m.pl."],["They heard the word of God.","This is a present participle with an enclitic."],["You all wrote the word of God.","<em>Šāmʿīn</em> means “hearing.”"]]},
{"after":1,"q":"Warm-up 4. What happens to the enclitic pronoun in the 3rd person plural present?","opts":[["It is not used: the plural ending <em>-īn</em>/<em>-ān</em> already marks the subject.","Right."],["It becomes a prefix.","There is no prefix in the participle."],["It is doubled.","No."],["It changes to <em>-tūn</em>.","<em>-tūn</em> is 2nd person plural."]]},
{"after":1,"q":"Warm-up 5. Write “She is writing” with <em>k-t-b</em>.","opts":[["<em>Kātbā-hī</em> (or just <em>Kātbā</em>)","Right."],["<em>Kāteb-hī</em>","<em>Kāteb</em> is masculine."],["<em>Ketbat</em>","That is the Perfect “she wrote.”"],["<em>Kātbīn</em>","That is masculine plural."]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 1. Identify ܟܬܒܘ (<em>ktabū</em>).","opts":[["3 m.pl. “they wrote”","Right."],["3 m.sg. “he wrote”","That is <em>ktab</em>."],["2 m.pl. “you wrote”","That is <em>ktabtūn</em>."],["1 c.pl. “we wrote”","That is <em>ktabn</em>."]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 1. Identify ܫܒܩܬ (<em>šbaqt</em>).","opts":[["2 m.sg. “you left”","Right."],["3 f.sg. “she left”","That is <em>šebqat</em>."],["1 c.pl. “we left”","That is <em>šbaqn</em>."],["3 m.pl. “they left”","That is <em>šbaqū</em>."]],"explain":"Unvocalized ܫܒܩܬ could also be 1 c.sg. <em>šebqet</em> “I left”; the exercise specifies 2 m.sg."},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 1. Identify ܢܛܪܬ (<em>neṭrat</em>).","opts":[["3 f.sg. “she kept”","Right."],["2 m.sg. “you kept”","That is <em>nṭart</em>."],["3 m.sg. “he kept”","That is <em>nṭar</em>."],["3 m.pl. “they kept”","That is <em>nṭarū</em>."]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 1. Identify ܥܪܩܢ (<em>ʿraqn</em>).","opts":[["1 c.pl. “we fled”","Right."],["3 f.pl. “they fled”","Not the Peal Perfect ending here; <em>-n</em> marks “we.”"],["1 c.sg. “I fled”","That is <em>ʿerqet</em>."],["2 m.pl. “you fled”","That is <em>ʿraqtūn</em>."]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 2. <em>p-l-ḥ</em>: “He served.”","opts":[["<em>plaḥ</em>","Right."],["<em>plaḥū</em>","That is “they served.”"],["<em>pelḥet</em>","That is “I served.”"],["<em>pāleḥ</em>","That is the participle “serving.”"]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 2. <em>p-l-ḥ</em>: “They (m) served.”","opts":[["<em>plaḥū</em>","Right."],["<em>plaḥtūn</em>","That is “you all served.”"],["<em>plaḥ</em>","That is “he served.”"],["<em>pelḥat</em>","That is “she served.”"]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 2. <em>p-l-ḥ</em>: “I served.”","opts":[["<em>pelḥet</em>","Right."],["<em>plaḥt</em>","That is “you (m.sg) served.”"],["<em>plaḥn</em>","That is “we served.”"],["<em>pelḥat</em>","That is “she served.”"]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 2. <em>p-l-ḥ</em>: “You all (m) served.”","opts":[["<em>plaḥtūn</em>","Right."],["<em>plaḥū</em>","That is “they served.”"],["<em>plaḥtēn</em>","That is feminine plural."],["<em>plaḥt</em>","That is singular."]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 3. Translate: <em>W-šbaq Yūḥannan l-malkā.</em>","opts":[["And Yukhannan left the king.","Right."],["And the king left Yukhannan.","<em>l-</em> marks <em>malkā</em> as the object."],["And Yukhannan is leaving the king.","<em>Šbaq</em> is Perfect."],["And Yukhannan wrote to the king.","<em>Šbaq</em> means “leave.”"]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 3. Translate: <em>Rdapū talmīdē l-bīšā.</em>","opts":[["The disciples pursued the evil man.","Right."],["The evil man pursued the disciples.","<em>l-</em> marks the object, <em>bīšā</em>."],["The disciple pursued the evil man.","<em>Rdapū</em> and <em>talmīdē</em> are plural."],["The disciples fled from the evil man.","“Fled” is <em>ʿraq</em>."]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 3. Translate: <em>Npaq malkā dēn men tarʿā.</em>","opts":[["But the king went out from the gate.","Right: <em>dēn</em> “but.”"],["And the king went in through the gate.","<em>Npaq</em> is “went out,” and <em>dēn</em> is “but.”"],["The king is going out from the gate.","<em>Npaq</em> is Perfect."],["But the king went out from the kingdom.","<em>Tarʿā</em> is “gate.”"]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 3. Translate: <em>Ktabn meltā d-Alāhā.</em>","opts":[["We wrote the word of God.","Right."],["They wrote the word of God.","That is <em>ktabū</em>."],["We are writing the word of God.","<em>Ktabn</em> is Perfect."],["I wrote the word of God.","That is <em>ketbet</em>."]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 4. Render (VSO): “The evil man fled from the light.”","opts":[["<em>ʿRaq barnāšā bīšā men nūhrā.</em>","Right."],["<em>Barnāšā bīšā ʿāraq men nūhrā.</em>","That is a present participle in SV order."],["<em>ʿRaq barnāšā bīšā l-nūhrā.</em>","“From” is <em>men</em>."],["<em>ʿRaqū barnāšā bīšā men nūhrā.</em>","The subject is singular."]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 4. Render: “And Yukhannan kept the word of God.”","opts":[["<em>W-nṭar Yūḥannan meltā d-Alāhā.</em>","Right."],["<em>W-nṭarū Yūḥannan meltā d-Alāhā.</em>","The subject is singular."],["<em>W-ktab Yūḥannan meltā d-Alāhā.</em>","<em>Ktab</em> is “wrote.”"],["<em>W-nāṭar Yūḥannan meltā d-Alāhā.</em>","That is the participle."]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 4. Render: “When the disciples drew near, they worshipped.”","opts":[["<em>Kad qrebū talmīdē, sgadū.</em>","Right."],["<em>Kad qreb talmīdē, sgad.</em>","The disciples are plural."],["<em>W-qrebū talmīdē, sgadū.</em>","“When” is <em>kad</em>."],["<em>Kad sgadū talmīdē, qrebū.</em>","The clauses are swapped."]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 4. Render: “The great king saved the earth.”","opts":[["<em>Praq malkā rabbā l-ʾarʿā.</em>","Right."],["<em>Praq malkā ṭābā l-ʾarʿā.</em>","<em>Ṭābā</em> is “good.”"],["<em>Praqū malkā rabbā l-ʾarʿā.</em>","The subject is singular."],["<em>Praq ʾarʿā l-malkā rabbā.</em>","That says the earth saved the king."]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 5 (Section 7). Whom did Yukhannan leave behind when he went out?","opts":[["His disciples (<em>talmīdāw-hy</em>)","Right."],["The king","Re-read Section 7."],["His brother","Re-read Section 7."],["The guards","Re-read Section 7."]]},
{"after":8,"q":"Exercise 5. What did the king’s “great one” do?","opts":[["He pursued (<em>rdap</em>) Yukhannan.","Right."],["He worshipped Yukhannan.","Re-read Section 7."],["He wrote a word.","Re-read Section 7."],["He closed the gate.","Re-read Section 7."]]},
